<%#
  No sandbox for this chat yet. The panel says which half is missing instead
  of showing an empty shell: a conversation gets its workspace the first time
  the agent runs something, and that needs the manager and the daemon.
-%>
<%
  health = Workspaces::Provider.available?
%>
<div class="card space-y-3">
  <p class="text-[13px] font-semibold text-fg">
    <% if stopped %>
      Workspace stopped
    <% else %>
      <%= health[:manager] && health[:docker] ? "No workspace yet" : "Execution is unavailable" %>
    <% end %>
  </p>

  <p class="text-[12px] leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">
    <% if stopped %>
      <%= stopped.name %> was destroyed on <%= stopped.updated_at.strftime("%Y-%m-%d at %H:%M") %>.
      Its container, its volume and its preview link are gone, so nothing here can
      be run or downloaded again. Ask the agent to start the work over and it
      will create a new sandbox for this chat.
    <% elsif !health[:manager] %>
      The workspace manager is not answering on this machine, so nothing can be
      created, run or previewed. Start it with
      <code class="font-mono text-[11px] text-fg">docker compose -f deploy/compose.workspaces.yml up -d</code>.
    <% elsif !health[:docker] %>
      The manager is up, but the Docker daemon behind it is not answering. Until
      it is, the agent will report that it could not run your request rather than
      pretend it did.
    <% elsif conversation.nil? %>
      This panel needs a conversation to look at. Open a chat and ask the agent
      to build something.
    <% else %>
      This conversation has not run anything yet. Ask the agent to write or run
      code and it will create a sandbox for this chat, do the work inside it, and
      show up here.
    <% end %>
  </p>
</div>
